\details{
Because the function has to estimate the species-specific coefficients/dispersion parameters for each species in \code{new_y}, then it is not true "marginal" hard-classification. Put another way, the resulting classifications are conditional on nuisance parameters estimated from the same response data, and so will be slightly optimistic.
